WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.034
-Good evening,
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.203
This is "Late Night."

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.437
We're so happy
to be with you this evening,

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.705
and now we're gonna
get to the news.

00:00:06.705 --> 00:00:07.941
President Biden yesterday

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:11.744
held a 1 hour and 51 minute
press conference.

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.680
It was the first thing
Americans actually wish

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.649
Joe Manchin had stopped.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.720
During his press conference
yesterday, President Biden said

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.057
Republicans were responsible
for some of his stalled agenda

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:27.893
and added, "I honest to God
don't know what they're for."

00:00:27.893 --> 00:00:31.464
Of course, that's the same thing
he said about Airpods.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.032
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.633
Today is the one-year
anniversary

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.402
of President Biden's
inauguration,

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:40.073
and he's not gonna like
Amanda Gorman's new poem.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:41.941
"There once was a man
named Joe Biden

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.542
whose office
he usually cried in."

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:46.546
All right, that's enough!

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.182
President Biden said yesterday
that his first year in office

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.417
has been "a year of challenges."

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.888
But he'd rather focus on the
positives, like your COVID test.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.190
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.994
I can make it,
because I've had it now!

00:01:04.463 --> 00:01:06.966
The Supreme Court
voted 8-1 yesterday

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.068
in favor of releasing
former President Trump's

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.336
White House records.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:14.206
The House committee
investigating the January attack

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.109
on the Capitol -- 8-1.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.877
This may be the first
recorded instance

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:21.781
of Donald Trump
inspiring bipartisanship.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.582
Former President Trump
said yesterday

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.051
that House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.620
should be banned
from trading stocks,

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.589
which brings us
to a segment called,

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.825
"Ah, Dammit,
I Agree With Trump."

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.928 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:38.831
Man, there is nothing worse
than hearing a Trump opinion

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:41.700
and thinking,
"The man's got a point."

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.436
But dammit, I agree with Trump.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.271
The only other time
this has happened

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:49.341
was when he said Ted Cruz
might be the Zodiac Killer.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:50.843
Oh, wait, I forgot.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.311
Also, that press conference
where he said

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.814
McDonald's breakfast
should be all day.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:59.151
-This has been
"Dammit, I Agree With Trump."

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:01.788
-A British judge
recently ordered a neo-Nazi

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:06.425
convicted of terror charges
to read classic literature

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:09.061
as part of his sentence,
including Jane Austen's

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.296
"Pride and Prejudice."

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.964
Said the neo-Nazi, "Sweet!

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.833
My two favorite things!"

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.969
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.372
Former President Trump --

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.807
They say "sweet" a lot.

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:23.609
People don't know that
about neo-Nazis,

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.144
but they're like, "Sweet!"

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:27.980
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.116
[ Laughs ]

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.684
Former President Trump
is currently on a media tour

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:35.721
promoting his new photo book
"Our Journey Together,"

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:38.891
and he's already being sued
by iPhoto.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:44.596
And finally, a wildlife YouTuber
on a trip to Thailand

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:47.099
recently discovered
a new species of tarantula

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:48.767
that lives inside
of bamboo plants.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.805
Yikes, that is a terrifying
thought that that even exists --

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.341
a wildlife YouTuber, I mean.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.243
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.945
And that was
the monologue, everybody!

